{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on rental property owner use of coordinator services","requirement":"A rental property owner, or any agent, representative, or subcontractor thereof, shall not receive, subscribe to, contract for, or otherwise exchange any form of consideration in return for the use of the services of a coordinator.","key_value":"prohibited_actor=rental_property_owner; prohibited_conduct=receive/subscribe/contract/exchange consideration for coordinator services","coverage_conditions":"Applies to rental property owners and their agents, representatives, or subcontractors. 'Coordinator' means any person who operates algorithmic revenue management software or an algorithmic device that performs a coordinating function for any rental property owner, including a rental property owner performing a coordinating function for their own benefit; 'coordinator' does not include a government entity that sets or limits rents or sale prices through affordability controls in accordance with law.","applicability":{"actor":"rental property owner, agent, representative, or subcontractor","conduct":"receive, subscribe to, contract for, or exchange consideration for use of coordinator services","subject":"residential dwelling units (excluding inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, or detention/correctional facilities)","geography":"New Jersey"},"exemptions":"'Coordinator' does not include a government entity that sets or limits rents or sale prices through affordability controls in accordance with law.","penalty":"Violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act; sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply pursuant to section 5.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c.043, §4(a)","quoted_span":"a.     a rental property owner, or any agent,
representative, or subcontractor thereof, to receive, subscribe to, contract
for, or otherwise exchange any form of consideration in return for the use of,
the services of a coordinator;","interaction":"Supplements and does not limit the New Jersey Antitrust Act, P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on coordinator facilitating anticompetitive agreement","requirement":"A coordinator shall not facilitate a tacit or express agreement among rental property owners that restricts competition with respect to residential dwelling units, including by performing a coordinating function.","key_value":"prohibited_actor=coordinator; prohibited_conduct=facilitate tacit or express agreement restricting competition; subject=residential dwelling units","coverage_conditions":"Applies to coordinators. 'Coordinating function' includes: (1) collecting competitively sensitive information of two or more rental property owners to analyze/process through an algorithm or automated process used to set or recommend rental prices, material lease terms, or occupancy levels, including to train an algorithm; (2) setting such terms pursuant to an algorithm that analyzes/processes another owner's competitively sensitive information; (3) setting for or recommending to two or more owners such terms pursuant to the same or substantially similar algorithm facilitating parallel pricing coordination.","applicability":{"actor":"coordinator","conduct":"facilitate tacit or express agreement among rental property owners restricting competition","subject":"residential dwelling units (excluding inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, or detention/correctional facilities)","geography":"New Jersey"},"exemptions":"Coordinating function does not include: (1) research, statistical analysis, or testing where competitively sensitive information is not used to set/recommend prices, terms, fees, occupancy rates/levels, or other contract terms; (2) developing an estimated amount of rent made available to the public at no cost; (3) use of a real estate brokerage database available on equal terms to subscribers that lists properties for rent or sale but does not set/recommend rental prices, material lease terms, or occupancy rates/levels or collect competitively sensitive information to do so; (4) a government entity setting or limiting rents or sale prices through affordability controls in accordance with law. 'Coordinator' does not include a government entity that sets or limits rents or sale prices through affordability controls in accordance with law.","penalty":"Violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act; sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply pursuant to section 5.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c.043, §4(b)","quoted_span":"b.    a coordinator to facilitate a tacit or express

agreement among rental property owners that restricts competition with respect
to residential dwelling units, including by performing a coordinating
function;","interaction":"Supplements and does not limit the New Jersey Antitrust Act, P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on parallel pricing coordination","requirement":"Two or more persons shall not engage in or otherwise facilitate parallel pricing coordination.","key_value":"prohibited_actor=two or more persons; prohibited_conduct=engage in or facilitate parallel pricing coordination","coverage_conditions":"'Parallel pricing coordination' means a tacit or express agreement between two or more rental property owners to raise, change, maintain, or manipulate pricing for leasing reasonably interchangeable residential dwelling units, including agreements between a coordinator and multiple property owners.","applicability":{"actor":"two or more persons","conduct":"engage in or facilitate parallel pricing coordination","subject":"residential dwelling units (excluding inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, or detention/correctional facilities)","geography":"New Jersey"},"exemptions":"Conduct required by affordability controls is excluded from 'parallel pricing coordination'.","penalty":"Violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act; sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply pursuant to section 5.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c.043, §4(c)","quoted_span":"c.     two or more persons to engage in
