{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on coordinator agents engaging in parallel pricing coordination","requirement":"Any agent or representative of a coordinator or subcontractor thereof shall not engage in parallel pricing coordination.","key_value":"prohibited_actor=agent or representative of coordinator or subcontractor; prohibited_conduct=engage in parallel pricing coordination","coverage_conditions":"Applies to agents and representatives of coordinators and their subcontractors. 'Parallel pricing coordination' means a tacit or express agreement between two or more rental property owners to raise, change, maintain, or manipulate pricing for leasing reasonably interchangeable residential dwelling units, including agreements between a coordinator and multiple property owners.","applicability":{"actor":"agent or representative of coordinator or subcontractor","conduct":"engage in parallel pricing coordination","subject":"residential dwelling units (excluding inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, or detention/correctional facilities)","geography":"New Jersey"},"exemptions":"Conduct required by affordability controls is excluded from 'parallel pricing coordination'.","penalty":"Violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act; sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply pursuant to section 5.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c.043, §4(d)","quoted_span":"d.    any agent or representative of a coordinator or
subcontractor thereof to engage in parallel pricing coordination; or","interaction":"Supplements and does not limit the New Jersey Antitrust Act, P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition on performing a coordinating function","requirement":"Any person shall not perform a coordinating function.","key_value":"prohibited_actor=any person; prohibited_conduct=perform a coordinating function","coverage_conditions":"'Coordinating function' includes: (1) collecting competitively sensitive information of two or more rental property owners to analyze/process through an algorithm or automated process used to set or recommend rental prices, material lease terms, or occupancy levels, including to train an algorithm; (2) setting such terms pursuant to an algorithm that analyzes/processes another owner's competitively sensitive information; (3) setting for or recommending to two or more owners such terms pursuant to the same or substantially similar algorithm facilitating parallel pricing coordination. 'Algorithmic device' means a device that uses one or more algorithms to process or otherwise perform calculations of data, including data concerning rental prices, material lease terms, or occupancy levels.","applicability":{"actor":"any person","conduct":"perform a coordinating function","subject":"residential dwelling units (excluding inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, or detention/correctional facilities)","geography":"New Jersey"},"exemptions":"Coordinating function does not include: (1) research, statistical analysis, or testing where competitively sensitive information is not used in setting or recommending rental prices, material lease terms, fees, occupancy rates/levels, or other contract terms; (2) developing an estimated amount of rent made available to the public at no cost; (3) use of a real estate brokerage database available on equal terms to subscribers that lists properties for rent or sale but does not set/recommend rental prices, material lease terms, or occupancy rates/levels or collect competitively sensitive information to do so; (4) a government entity setting or limiting rents or sale prices through affordability controls in accordance with law. 'Algorithmic device' does not include a spreadsheet that operates without artificial intelligence and requires human analysis, or a database that only uses an algorithm to query unprocessed data stored on or within that database.","penalty":"Violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act; sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply pursuant to section 5.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c.043, §4(e)","quoted_span":"e.     any person to perform a coordinating function.","interaction":"Supplements and does not limit the New Jersey Antitrust Act, P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
